WEBVTT

00:00.628 --> 00:02.404
- [Voiceover] So we're told that f of x

00:02.404 --> 00:07.063
is equal to x over one
minus cosine of x minus two,

00:07.063 --> 00:09.195
and they ask us to select
the correct description

00:09.195 --> 00:13.312
of the one-sided limits
of f at x equals two.

00:13.312 --> 00:15.498
And we see that right at x equals two,

00:15.498 --> 00:18.623
if we try to evaluate f of two,

00:18.623 --> 00:22.018
we get two over one minus cosine

00:22.018 --> 00:23.435
of two minus two,

00:24.383 --> 00:28.478
which is the same thing as cosine of zero,

00:28.478 --> 00:31.601
and cosine of zero is just one,

00:31.601 --> 00:34.018
and so one minus one is zero,

00:34.910 --> 00:38.833
and so the function is not
defined at x equals two,

00:38.833 --> 00:41.364
and that's why it might be
interesting to find the limit

00:41.364 --> 00:44.177
as x approaches two, and
especially the one-sided limit.

00:44.177 --> 00:45.241
And the one-sided limit.

00:45.241 --> 00:46.666
Well, we'll obviously leave it at that

00:46.666 --> 00:48.568
so let's try to approach this.

00:48.568 --> 00:50.872
So there's actually a couple
of ways you could do it.

00:50.872 --> 00:52.994
There is one way you could
do this without a calculator

00:52.994 --> 00:55.618
by just inspecting what's going on here,

00:55.618 --> 00:58.098
and thinking about the properties
of the cosine function,

00:58.098 --> 01:00.526
and if that inspires you,
pause the video and work it out,

01:00.526 --> 01:02.503
and I will do that at
the end of this video.

01:02.503 --> 01:06.356
The other way, if you have a calculator

01:06.356 --> 01:08.035
is to do it with a little bit of a table

01:08.035 --> 01:09.824
like we've done in other example problems.

01:09.824 --> 01:13.235
So if we think about x approaching two

01:13.235 --> 01:16.954
from the positive direction, well then.

01:16.954 --> 01:18.778
We can make a little table here

01:18.778 --> 01:22.587
where you have x, and
then you have f of x.

01:22.587 --> 01:26.478
And so for approaching two
from values greater than two,

01:26.478 --> 01:28.061
you could have 2.1,

01:29.770 --> 01:30.603
2.01.

01:32.312 --> 01:33.629
Now the reason why I said calculators,

01:33.629 --> 01:35.662
these aren't trivial to evaluate

01:35.662 --> 01:38.245
because this would be what, 2.1

01:39.638 --> 01:41.555
over 1 minus cosine of,

01:42.428 --> 01:44.178
2.1 minus two is 0.1.

01:46.838 --> 01:50.083
I do not know what cosine of
0.1 is without a calculator.

01:50.083 --> 01:53.083
I do know that cosine of zero is one

01:54.576 --> 01:58.318
so this is very, very close
to one without getting to one,

01:58.318 --> 02:00.023
and it's going to be less than one.

02:00.023 --> 02:03.140
Cosine is never going
to be greater than one.

02:03.140 --> 02:05.616
The cosine function is
bounded between negative one

02:05.616 --> 02:07.699
is less than cosine of x.

02:09.069 --> 02:11.516
I'll just write the x, then
I don't need the parenthesis.

02:11.516 --> 02:13.766
Which is less than one.

02:13.766 --> 02:17.760
The cosine function just
oscillates between these two values

02:17.760 --> 02:20.880
so this, this thing is
gonna be approaching one

02:20.880 --> 02:22.467
but it's going to be less than one.

02:22.467 --> 02:25.081
It definitely cannot be greater than one,

02:25.081 --> 02:25.957
and that's actually a good hint

02:25.957 --> 02:28.154
for how you can just
explore the structure here,

02:28.154 --> 02:30.525
and then you could say, "All right, 2.01.

02:30.525 --> 02:32.373
"Well, that's going to be 2.01

02:32.373 --> 02:33.623
"over one minus

02:34.629 --> 02:36.046
"cosine of 0.01."

02:39.874 --> 02:42.969
And this is going to even closer to one

02:42.969 --> 02:47.314
without being one but it's
going to be less than one.

02:47.314 --> 02:48.873
No matter what, cosine of anything

02:48.873 --> 02:52.034
is going to be between
negative one and one,

02:52.034 --> 02:54.237
and it could even be
including those things

02:54.237 --> 02:56.817
but as we approach two,

02:56.817 --> 03:00.439
this thing is going to approach one,

03:00.439 --> 03:03.208
I guess you could say
approach one from below.

03:03.208 --> 03:05.119
And so you can start to
make some intuitions here.

03:05.119 --> 03:09.005
If it's approaching from
below, this thing over here,

03:09.005 --> 03:12.642
this whole expression
is going to be positive,

03:12.642 --> 03:15.346
and as we approach x equals two.

03:15.346 --> 03:16.555
Well, the numerator is positive.

03:16.555 --> 03:17.611
It's approaching two.

03:17.611 --> 03:20.539
The denominator is positive
so this whole thing

03:20.539 --> 03:23.049
has to be approaching a positive value

03:23.049 --> 03:24.387
or it could become unbounded

03:24.387 --> 03:26.008
in the positive direction as we'll see,

03:26.008 --> 03:29.008
this is unbounded because this thing

03:30.138 --> 03:32.379
is even closer to one than this thing,

03:32.379 --> 03:34.301
and you would see that
if you have a calculator

03:34.301 --> 03:36.715
but needless to say, this
is going to be unbounded

03:36.715 --> 03:39.554
in the positive direction
so we're going to be going

03:39.554 --> 03:43.426
towards positive infinity so
these two choices have that,

03:43.426 --> 03:47.531
and we can make the exact
same argument as we approach x

03:47.531 --> 03:50.305
in the negative or from below,

03:50.305 --> 03:53.126
as we approach two from
below, I should say.

03:53.126 --> 03:56.194
So that's x, and that is f of x,

03:56.194 --> 03:58.354
and once again, I don't have
a calculator in front of me.

03:58.354 --> 04:00.338
You could evaluate these
things at a calculator,

04:00.338 --> 04:02.287
and become very clear
that these are positive,

04:02.287 --> 04:03.624
and as we get closer to,

04:03.624 --> 04:06.632
they become even larger
and larger positive values,

04:06.632 --> 04:10.549
and the same thing would
happen if you did 1.9,

04:12.986 --> 04:14.569
and if you did 1.99

04:16.020 --> 04:20.103
because here, you'd be
1.9 over one minus cosine.

04:21.179 --> 04:23.500
Now here, you'd have 1.9 minus two

04:23.500 --> 04:26.000
so this would be negative 0.1.

04:27.610 --> 04:29.215
Let me scroll over a little bit.

04:29.215 --> 04:32.018
The second one would be 1.99

04:32.018 --> 04:33.768
over one minus cosine

04:34.680 --> 04:36.097
of negative 0.01.

04:39.559 --> 04:42.043
And cosine of negative 0.1

04:42.043 --> 04:44.088
is the same thing as cosine of 0.1.

04:44.088 --> 04:46.005
Cosine of negative 0.01

04:48.072 --> 04:51.111
is the same thing as cosine of 0.01.

04:51.111 --> 04:54.385
So these two things, this is
going to be equal to that.

04:54.385 --> 04:56.269
That is going to be equal to that.

04:56.269 --> 04:59.102
And once again, we're gonna be
approaching positive infinity

04:59.102 --> 05:01.227
so the only choice where
all of that is true

05:01.227 --> 05:03.517
is this first one.

05:03.517 --> 05:05.547
Whether we approach two
from the right-hand side

05:05.547 --> 05:08.510
or the left-hand side, we're
approaching positive infinity

05:08.510 --> 05:10.132
but the other way you could
have deduced that is say,

05:10.132 --> 05:11.902
"Okay, as we approach two,

05:11.902 --> 05:13.800
the numerator is going to be positive

05:13.800 --> 05:17.429
'cause two is positive,
and then over here,

05:17.429 --> 05:18.612
as we approach two,

05:18.612 --> 05:21.843
cosine of anything can
never be greater than one.

05:21.843 --> 05:24.617
It's going to approach
one but be less than one

05:24.617 --> 05:28.534
so if this is less than
as x approaches two.

05:29.675 --> 05:32.410
It becomes one when x is equal to two.

05:32.410 --> 05:34.173
Well then, this right over here,

05:34.173 --> 05:37.633
one minus something less than
one is going to be positive

05:37.633 --> 05:39.351
so you have a positive
divided by a positive

05:39.351 --> 05:41.857
so you're definitely going
to get positive values

05:41.857 --> 05:43.305
as you approach two.

05:43.305 --> 05:45.870
And we know, and they've already told us

05:45.870 --> 05:48.477
that these are going to be
unbounded based on the choices

05:48.477 --> 05:50.481
so you would also pick that

05:50.481 --> 05:51.943
but you should also feel good about it,

05:51.943 --> 05:55.068
that the closer that we get to two,

05:55.068 --> 05:59.235
the closer that this value
right over here gets to zero.

06:00.618 --> 06:02.335
And the closer that
this value gets to zero,

06:02.335 --> 06:03.842
the closer we get to one.

06:03.842 --> 06:07.883
The closer we get to one, the
smaller the denominator gets.

06:07.883 --> 06:10.077
And then you divide by smaller
and smaller denominators,

06:10.077 --> 06:12.908
you're going to become
unbounded towards infinity,

06:12.908 --> 06:15.857
which is exactly what we
see in that first choice.
